('nixie','Nixie','Nixie','1','Small','Fey (Aquatic)','Always neutral','1d6 (3 hp)',3,'+3','20 ft. (4 squares), swim 30 ft.','14 (+1 size, +3 Dex), touch 14, flat-footed 11','+0/–6','Short sword +4 melee (1d4–2/19–20) or light crossbow +4 ranged (1d6/19–20)','5 ft./5 ft.','+0','+5','+3',7,16,11,12,13,18,'Bluff +8, Craft (any one) +5, Escape Artist +6, Handle Animal +8, Hide +7*, Listen +6, Perform (sing) +7, Search +3, Sense Motive +5, Spot +6, Swim +6','DodgeB, Weapon Finesse','{"special_attacks":"Charm person","special_qualities":"Amphibious, damage reduction 5/cold iron, low-light vision, spell resistance 16, water breathing, wild empathy"}'::jsonb,'Most nixies are slim and comely, with lightly scaled, pale green skin and dark green hair. Females often twine shells and pearl strings in their hair and dress in wraps woven from colorful seaweed. Males wear loincloths of the same materials. Nixies prefer not to leave their lakes.

A nixie stands about 4 feet tall and weighs about 45 pounds.

