('treant','Treant','Treant','8','Huge','Plant','Usually neutral good','7d8+35 (66 hp)',66,'–1','30 ft. (6 squares)','20 (–2 size, –1 Dex, +13 natural), touch 7, flat-footed 20','+5/+22','Slam +12 melee (2d6+9)','15 ft./15 ft.','+10','+1','+7',29,8,21,12,16,12,'Diplomacy +3, Hide –9*, Intimidate +6, Knowledge (nature) +6, Listen +8, Sense Motive +8, Spot +8, Survival +8 (+10 aboveground)','Improved Sunder, Iron Will, Power Attack','{"special_attacks":"Animate trees, double damage against objects, trample 2d6+13","special_qualities":"Damage reduction 10/slashing, low-light vision, plant traits, vulnerability to fire"}'::jsonb,'A treant’s leaves are deep green in the spring and summer. In the fall and winter the leaves change to yellow, orange, or red, but they rarely fall out. A treant’s legs fit together when closed to look like the trunk of a tree, and a motionless treant is nearly indistinguishable from a tree.

A treant is about 30 feet tall, with a “trunk” about 2 feet in diameter. It weighs about 4,500 pounds.

Treants speak their own language, plus Common and Sylvan. Most also can manage a smattering of just about all other humanoid tongues—at least enough to say “Get away from my trees!”','{"full_attack":"2 slams +12 melee (2d6+9)","environment":"Temperate forests","organization":"Solitary or grove (4–7)","treasure":"Standard","advancement":"8–16 HD (Huge); 17–21 HD (Gargantuan)","level_adjustment":"+5","statblock":{"hit_dice":"7d8+35 (66 hp)","hit_points":66,"base_attack_grapple":"+5/+22","attack":"Slam +12 melee (2d6+9)","full_attack":"2 slams +12 melee (2d6+9)","space_reach":"15 ft./15 ft.","saves":"Fort +10, Ref +1, Will +7","abilities":{"str":"29","dex":"8","con":"21","int":"12","wis":"16","cha":"12"},"skills":"Diplomacy +3, Hide –9*, Intimidate +6, Knowledge (nature) +6, Listen +8, Sense Motive +8, Spot +8, Survival +8 (+10 aboveground)","feats":"Improved Sunder, Iron Will, Power Attack","special_attacks":"Animate trees, double damage against objects, trample 2d6+13","special_qualities":"Damage reduction 10/slashing, low-light vision, plant traits, vulnerability to fire"},"source_file":"monsters-t-z.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-t-z.html',true),
