('yrthak','Yrthak','Yrthak','9','Huge','Magical Beast','Often neutral','12d10+36 (102 hp)',102,'+6','20 ft. (4 squares), fly 60 ft. (average)','18 (–2 size, +2 Dex, +8 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 16','+12/+25','Bite +15 melee (2d8+5) or sonic lance +12 ranged touch (6d6)','15 ft./10 ft.','+11','+10','+5',20,14,17,7,13,11,'Listen +12, Move Silently +10','Endurance, Flyby Attack, Improved Initiative, Multiattack, Snatch','{"special_attacks":"Sonic lance, explosion","special_qualities":"Blindsight 120 ft., immunities, vulnerability to sonic"}'::jsonb,'A yrthak is blind. It senses sound and movement by means of a special organ on its long tongue. It emits powerfully focused beams of sound from the protrusion on its head. The creature is a yellowish-green color, with the wings and fin being more yellow and the head and body more green. The teeth are yellow.

A yrthak is about 20 feet long, with a wingspan of 40 feet. It weighs about 5,000 pounds.

Despite their intelligence, yrthaks do not speak.','{"full_attack":"Bite +15 melee (2d8+5) and 2 claws +13 melee (1d6+2); or sonic lance +12 ranged touch (6d6)","environment":"Temperate mountains","organization":"Solitary or clutch (2–4)","treasure":"None","advancement":"13–16 HD (Huge); 17–36 HD (Gargantuan)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"12d10+36 (102 hp)","hit_points":102,"base_attack_grapple":"+12/+25","attack":"Bite +15 melee (2d8+5) or sonic lance +12 ranged touch (6d6)","full_attack":"Bite +15 melee (2d8+5) and 2 claws +13 melee (1d6+2); or sonic lance +12 ranged touch (6d6)","space_reach":"15 ft./10 ft.","saves":"Fort +11, Ref +10, Will +5","abilities":{"str":"20","dex":"14","con":"17","int":"7","wis":"13","cha":"11"},"skills":"Listen +12, Move Silently +10","feats":"Endurance, Flyby Attack, Improved Initiative, Multiattack, Snatch","special_attacks":"Sonic lance, explosion","special_qualities":"Blindsight 120 ft., immunities, vulnerability to sonic"},"source_file":"monsters-t-z.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-t-z.html',true),
