('giant_ant_queen','Giant Ant, Queen','Giant Ant, Queen','2','Large','Vermin','','4d8+4 (22 hp)',22,'–1','40 ft. (8 squares)','17 (–1 size, –1 Dex, +9 natural), touch 8, flat-footed 17','+3/+10','Bite +5 melee (2d6+4)','10 ft./5 ft.','+5','+0','+2',16,9,13,null,13,11,'—','TrackB','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Scent, vermin traits"}'::jsonb,'Giant ants are among the hardiest and most adaptable vermin. Soldiers and workers are about 6 feet long, while queens can grow to a length of 9 feet.

**Acid Sting (Ex):** A giant soldier ant has a stinger and an acid-producing gland in its abdomen. If it successfully grabs an opponent, it can attempt to sting each round (+3 attack bonus). A hit with the sting attack deals 1d4+1 points of piercing damage and 1d4 points of acid damage.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a giant ant must hit with its bite attack. A giant soldier ant that wins the ensuing grapple check establishes a hold and can sting.

**Skills:** \*Giant ants have a +4 racial bonus on Survival checks when tracking by scent and a +8 racial bonus on Climb checks. A giant ant can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened.','{"full_attack":"Bite +5 melee (2d6+4)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Hive (1 plus 10–100 workers and 5–20 soldiers)","treasure":"1/10 coins; 50% goods; 50% items","advancement":"5–6 HD (Large); 7–8 HD (Huge)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"4d8+4 (22 hp)","hit_points":22,"base_attack_grapple":"+3/+10","attack":"Bite +5 melee (2d6+4)","full_attack":"Bite +5 melee (2d6+4)","space_reach":"10 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +5, Ref +0, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"16","dex":"9","con":"13","int":null,"wis":"13","cha":"11"},"skills":"—","feats":"TrackB","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Scent, vermin traits"},"source_file":"monsters-vermin.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-vermin.html',true),
('giant_bee','Giant Bee','Giant Bee','1','Medium','Vermin','','3d8 (13 hp)',13,'+2','20 ft. (4 squares), fly 80 ft. (good)','14 (+2 Dex, +2 natural), touch 12, flat-footed 12','+2/+2','Sting +2 melee (1d4 plus poison)','5 ft./5 ft.','+3','+3','+2',11,14,11,null,12,9,'Spot +5, Survival +1*','—','{"special_attacks":"Poison","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., vermin traits"}'::jsonb,'Although many times larger, growing to a length of about 5 feet, giant bees behave generally the same as their smaller cousins. Giant bees are usually not aggressive except when defending themselves or their hive.

**Poison (Ex):** Injury, Fortitude DC 11, initial and secondary damage 1d4 Con. The save DC is Constitution-based. A giant bee that successfully stings another creature pulls away, leaving its stinger in the creature. The bee then dies.

**Skills:** Giant bees have a +4 racial bonus on Spot checks. \*They also have a +4 racial bonus on Survival checks to orient themselves.','{"full_attack":"Sting +2 melee (1d4 plus poison)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Solitary, buzz (2–5), or hive (11–20)","treasure":"No coins; 1/4 goods (honey only); no items","advancement":"4–6 HD (Medium); 7–9 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"3d8 (13 hp)","hit_points":13,"base_attack_grapple":"+2/+2","attack":"Sting +2 melee (1d4 plus poison)","full_attack":"Sting +2 melee (1d4 plus poison)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +3, Will +2","abilities":{"str":"11","dex":"14","con":"11","int":null,"wis":"12","cha":"9"},"skills":"Spot +5, Survival +1*","feats":"—","special_attacks":"Poison","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., vermin traits"},"source_file":"monsters-vermin.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-vermin.html',true),
('giant_bombardier_beetle','Giant Bombardier Beetle','Giant Bombardier Beetle','2','Medium','Vermin','','2d8+4 (13 hp)',13,'+0','30 ft. (6 squares)','16 (+6 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 16','+1/+2','Bite +2 melee (1d4+1)','5 ft./5 ft.','+5','+0','+0',13,10,14,null,10,9,'—','—','{"special_attacks":"Acid spray","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., vermin traits"}'::jsonb,'These creatures feed primarily on carrion and offal, gathering heaps of the stuff in which to build nests and lay eggs. A giant bombardier beetle is about 6 feet long. Giant bombardier beetles normally attack only to defend themselves, their nests, or their eggs.

